dictation-app

This product includes or depends on the following third-party software.

handy-keys 0.3.4 (https://github.com/handy-computer/handy-keys)
  Global keyboard listener behind the macOS hotkey
  (crates/platform/src/hotkey/macos.rs). Used as a dependency; no code
  copied.
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 handy-computer

handy-recorder 0.1.0 (https://github.com/handy-computer/handy-recorder)
  Microphone capture behind the macOS audio adapter
  (crates/platform/src/audio/macos.rs): the CoreAudio callback, lock-free
  ring buffer, mono mix and resampling to 16 kHz. Used as a dependency; no
  code copied. Its own dependencies include handy-cpal 0.18.2
  (Apache-2.0), rubato 5.0.0 and rtrb 0.4.1 (MIT OR Apache-2.0).
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 handy-computer

objc2, block2, objc2-av-foundation (https://github.com/madsmtm/objc2)
  The macOS microphone permission check and prompt
  (crates/platform/src/permissions/macos.rs). Used as dependencies.
  MIT License (objc2, block2); objc2-av-foundation under
  Zlib OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT.

Ideas only, no code: Handy (MIT) for keeping the microphone open briefly
between dictations; Muesli (MIT) for never waiting on CoreAudio from the
thread that drives the UI and for treating route changes as a reason to
reopen the device.
